{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.Observation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.Observation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CRRealisation","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L93-L93","doc":"**Well-definedness from observability**: the adjoint vanishing\n`H⁰(M, Ad(P)) = 0` ensures all sections are gauge-equivalent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_gauge_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_gauge_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L90-L90","doc":"`obs` is constant on gauge-equivalence classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.gaugeEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.gaugeEquiv","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Gauge equivalence relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The observation map `obs : Γ(S) → ℝ`.\n\nWas `StateSections → R_q` while this very docstring said `→ ℝ`, and the\nstructure is named **Archimedean**Observation with the label\n`rem:observation-archimedean`. The library copy\n(`lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean:250`) always had\n`ℝ`. Bean `qou-u87j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.StateSections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.StateSections","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The type of global sections `Γ(S)` of the state bundle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation","kind":"structure","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L72-L93","doc":"**Archimedean observation**: concrete realisation of `Observation` on a\nCR manifold as a gauge-equivariant endomorphism of the state bundle.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:observation-archimedean}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.substrate_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.substrate_shift","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L69-L69","doc":"**Substrate perturbation** `δq`, carried as a morphism `𝟙 → 𝟙`.\n\nScope warning: this is *free data*, not a derived quantity.  The\nnarrative describes `δq` as **determined by** the Hopf coaction, but\nnothing in this structure ties `substrate_shift` either to\n`qou.frobHopf`'s comultiplication or to `morphism` — any endomorphism\nof the unit inhabits the field.  Deriving it (or constraining it by a\ncoaction equation) is open; until then do not read an inhabitant of\n`Observation` as evidence that the shift is coaction-induced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.frobenius_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.frobenius_compat","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L58-L58","doc":"**Frobenius compatibility**: `λ ∘ O = λ` — the observation preserves\nthe Frobenius form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.morphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.morphism","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The observation morphism `O : A → A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L46-L70","doc":"**Observation** as a categorical endomorphism `O : A → A` in `C`.\n\nAn observation preserves the Frobenius form and induces a substrate\nperturbation `q ↦ q + δq` via the Hopf coaction.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:observation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation.lean#L36-L38","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}